msgid ""
"The FV() function returns a value that consist of the present value plus "
"multiples periods of interest. If you have $1000 on your bank account, and "
"you get 8% interest then after two years the amount of money you will own is "
"FV( 1000; 0.08; 2 ). That means FV calculates the future value of your "
"money, that it why it is called FV."
msgstr ""

