#: xml_doc.cc:422
msgid ""
"The PV() function returns the value that you need if you want to reach the "
"future value after a certain amount of periods and a certain interest. For "
"example if you need $1166.40 for your new computer and you want to buy it in "
"two years while getting an interest of 8% then PV( 1166.4; 0.08; 2 ) tells "
"you how much money you need now, in the presence. PV calculates the present "
"value that you need to reach a future value, that is why it is called PV."
msgstr ""

#: xml_doc.cc:423
msgid "PV( future_value; interest; periods )"
msgstr ""

#: xml_doc.cc:424
msgid "PV( 1166.4; 0.08; 2 ) equals 1000"
