#: xml_doc.cc:430
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The PV_annuity() function tells you how much cash you need today (in the "
"presence) if you want to reach a certain cash volume in the future. We "
"assume that you put every month a certain amount of money on your bank "
"account which gives you a certain interest. Now you wonder how much money "
"your bank account must have initially so that you have a certain amount of "
"money after some periods. Lets give a concrete example: You need $1374.40 in "
"two years. At the end of each year you add $100 your account and you have 8% "
"interest. Then PV_annuity( 100; 0.08; 2; 1374.4; FALSE ) tells you that your "
"bank account must have $1000 initially. In case you pay the $100 not at the "
"end of the year, but in the beginning, you would choose TRUE as the last "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

